vef|n|The spirit; the soul of man. ; The disembodied soul; the soul or spirit of a deceased person; a spirit appearing after death; an apparition; a specter. ; Any faint shadowy semblance; an unsubstantial image; a phantom; a glimmering; as, not a ghost of a chance; the ghost of an idea. ; A false image formed in a telescope by reflection from the surfaces of one or more lenses.	N:16eo,56,7~16eo,56,7
